Cell[BoxData["\<\"In flat space, \\!\\(\\*SuperscriptBox[\\(ds\\), \
\\(2\\)]\\) = \\!\\(\\*SuperscriptBox[\\(dr\\), \\(2\\)]\\); i.e., the radial \
distance r equals the proper distance s. In curved space, they are not the \
same. Hence, to check whether the \\!\\(\\*SubscriptBox[\\(\[Psi]\\), \
\\(5\\)]\\) circle shrinks smoothly down to zero, we have to use the proper \
distance, s.\"\>"], "Print",
