\\!\\(\\*SuperscriptBox[\\(ds\\), \\(2\\)]\\) gets large and the \
\\!\\(\\*SubscriptBox[\\(\[GothicCapitalD]\\), \
\\(5\\)]\\)\\!\\(\\*SuperscriptBox[SubscriptBox[\\(p\\), \\(5\\)], \
\\(2\\)]\\)\\!\\(\\*SuperscriptBox[SubscriptBox[\\(d\[Psi]\\), \\(5\\)], \\(2\
\\)]\\) term gets small, so that \\!\\(\\*SuperscriptBox[\\(ds\\), \
\\(2\\)]\\) \[TildeTilde] \\!\\(\\*FractionBox[SuperscriptBox[\\(dr\\), \
\\(2\\)], \\(\\(\\*SubscriptBox[\\(\[GothicCapitalD]\\), \
\\(5\\)]\\)[r]\\)]\\) = \\!\\(\\*FractionBox[SuperscriptBox[\\(dr\\), \
\\(2\\)], \\(1 + \\*FractionBox[\\(\[Chi]\\), \\(r\\)]\\)]\\). This is the \
metric we use to determine whether the pinch has a sharp point or is \
smooth.\"\>"], "Print",
