Cell[BoxData["\<\"With \[Chi]=-\\!\\(\\*FractionBox[SubscriptBox[\\(p\\), \
\\(5\\)], \\(2\\)]\\) the bottom is rounded (smooth); with \
\[Chi]=-\\!\\(\\*SubscriptBox[\\(p\\), \\(5\\)]\\) it comes to a\\nsharp \
point (a cone). The claim below show that \
\[Chi]=-\\!\\(\\*FractionBox[SubscriptBox[\\(p\\), \\(5\\)], \\(2\\)]\\) is \
the only value\\nthat gives a smooth bottom. (Note: the plot uses \
\\!\\(\\*SubscriptBox[\\(p\\), \\(5\\)]\\)=1.)\"\>"], "Print",
 CellChangeTimes->{
