Cell[BoxData["\<\"(1) To claim smoothness, the full \
\\!\\(\\*SuperscriptBox[\\(ds\\), \\(2\\)]\\) line element involving t, r, \
\[Theta], \[Phi], \\!\\(\\*SubscriptBox[\\(\[Psi]\\), \\(4\\)]\\), and \\!\\(\
\\*SubscriptBox[\\(\[Psi]\\), \\(5\\)]\\) must be considered. The transverse \
line element used to prove the claim involves just r and \
\\!\\(\\*SubscriptBox[\\(\[Psi]\\), \\(5\\)]\\). However since there are no \
off-diagonal metric terms \\!\\(\\*SubscriptBox[\\(g\\), \
\\(\[Mu]\[Nu]\\)]\\), there is no mixing of different directions. \
Consequently, the entire 6D spacetime is smooth if the transverse space is.\"\
\>"], "Print",
 CellChangeTimes->{
