Cell[BoxData["\<\"As pointed out earlier, \[ScriptCapitalA](t) = \
\\!\\(\\*SuperscriptBox[\\(c\\), \\(2\\)]\\) is simply a rearrangement of the \
continuity equation. Since the a(t) formula in Part a is the result of \
solving \[ScriptCapitalA](t) = \\!\\(\\*SuperscriptBox[\\(c\\), \\(2\\)]\\), \
the 4-branch a(t) formula is also the solution to the Friedmann \
equations.\"\>"], "Print",
 CellChangeTimes->{
